## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the `pcapng file` from challenge using `wget`.
2. Open wireshark, click file at `top left and click open` and choose the `pcapng file`.
3. Press Ctrl + F.
4. Change the first dropdown to Packet bytes.
5. Change the second dropdown to Regular Expression.
6. Type this into the search box: [a-zA-Z]{7}\{[a-zA-Z0-9_]+\}
7. Click Find.
8. This regex pattern tells Wireshark to look for any 7 letters followed by { and }, which perfectly matches the format of picoCTF{...} even if the letters themselves are completely scrambled by ROT13.
9. Convert the scrambled text into normal text using `cyberchef(rot13)` or echo command.
10. The flag will be displayed.



